---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import CtaSection from '../components/CtaSection.astro';
---
<BaseLayout title="Silk Road Visa Guide — China & Central Asia Travel Visas" description="Complete Silk Road visa guide: China tourist visa (L), 144-hour transit-free, Central Asia e-visas (Uzbekistan, Kyrgyzstan, Kazakhstan, Tajikistan, Turkmenistan, Mongolia, Pakistan). Invitation letters provided." ogImage="/assets/images/hero-silkroad.jpg">
<div class="visa-hero" style="background:linear-gradient(rgba(0,0,0,.55),rgba(0,0,0,.55)),url('/assets/images/hero-silkroad.jpg') center/cover;">
  <div class="container">
    <h1>Silk Road Visa Guide</h1>
    <p>Everything you need to know about visas for China and Central Asia — from tourist visas to transit-free policies and e-visas. We provide free invitation letters for all confirmed bookings.</p>
  </div>
</div>

<script type="application/ld+json">
{
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@type": "BreadcrumbList",
  "itemListElement": [
    { "@type": "ListItem", "position": 1, "name": "Home", "item": "https://silkroadwondertours.com/" },
    { "@type": "ListItem", "position": 2, "name": "Visa Guide" }
  ]
}
</script>
<nav class="breadcrumb" aria-label="Breadcrumb"><div class="container"><a href="/">Home</a> <span class="sep">/</span> <span>Visa Guide</span></div></nav>

<!-- China Visa Section -->
<section class="section"><div class="container">
  <div class="section-header reveal">
    <h2>China Tourist Visa (L Visa)</h2>
    <div class="divider"></div>
    <p>The essential guide to obtaining your Chinese tourist visa for the Silk Road</p>
  </div>

  <p style="font-size:1.05rem;line-height:1.7;max-width:860px;margin:0 auto 32px;">For most international travelers, a China Tourist Visa (L visa) is required to explore the Silk Road routes through Xinjiang, Gansu, Qinghai, and other Chinese provinces. The standard L visa allows a stay of 30-90 days with single, double, or multiple entries. As a registered Chinese travel agency, <strong>Silk Road Wonders provides official invitation letters for all confirmed tour bookings at no additional cost</strong> — a critical document that significantly strengthens your visa application.</p>

  <h3 style="font-family:var(--font-display);font-size:1.3rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:16px;">Application Steps</h3>
  
  <div class="visa-step"><div class="visa-step-num">1</div><div class="visa-step-body"><h4>Prepare Your Passport</h4><p>Your passport must be valid for at least 6 months beyond your planned entry date into China and have at least 2 blank visa pages.</p></div></div>
  <div class="visa-step"><div class="visa-step-num">2</div><div class="visa-step-body"><h4>Complete the Application Form</h4><p>Fill out the China Online Visa Application (COVA) form at the official Chinese Visa Application Service Center (CVASC) website. The form is available in English and several other languages.</p></div></div>
  <div class="visa-step"><div class="visa-step-num">3</div><div class="visa-step-body"><h4>Gather Supporting Documents</h4><p>Prepare: recent passport photo (48mm x 33mm, white background), round-trip flight itinerary, hotel reservations or our invitation letter, proof of financial means (bank statements), and travel insurance documentation.</p></div></div>
  <div class="visa-step"><div class="visa-step-num">4</div><div class="visa-step-body"><h4>Submit Your Application</h4><p>Visit your nearest Chinese Visa Application Service Center (CVASC) in person. Most countries require in-person submission with biometric data collection. Processing takes 4-10 business days (standard) or 2-3 days (express, additional fee).</p></div></div>
  <div class="visa-step"><div class="visa-step-num">5</div><div class="visa-step-body"><h4>Receive Your Visa</h4><p>Collect your passport with the visa sticker. Double-check all details: name spelling, passport number, entry dates, and number of entries. Contact the consulate immediately if you find any errors.</p></div></div>

  <div class="visa-note">
    <strong>&#128161; Pro Tip:</strong> Apply for a <strong>multiple-entry visa</strong> if your Silk Road itinerary includes side trips to Central Asian countries (Uzbekistan, Kyrgyzstan, Kazakhstan) with returns to China. A double-entry visa is the minimum recommended for cross-border Silk Road itineraries. We recommend applying at least <strong>6 weeks before departure</strong>.
  </div>

  <h3 style="font-family:var(--font-display);font-size:1.3rem;color:var(--navy);margin:32px 0 16px;">China Visa Fees (Approximate, USD)</h3>
  <table class="visa-table">
    <tr><th>Nationality</th><th>Single Entry</th><th>Double Entry</th><th>Multiple Entry (6mo)</th><th>Multiple Entry (12mo)</th></tr>
    <tr><td>USA</td><td>$185</td><td>$185</td><td>$185</td><td>$185</td></tr>
    <tr><td>UK</td><td>$130</td><td>$130</td><td>$130</td><td>$260</td></tr>
    <tr><td>EU Countries</td><td>$85-130</td><td>$85-130</td><td>$85-130</td><td>$170-260</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Canada</td><td>$100</td><td>$100</td><td>$100</td><td>$100</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Australia</td><td>$85</td><td>$85</td><td>$85</td><td>$170</td></tr>
    <tr><td>India</td><td>$30</td><td>$45</td><td>$60</td><td>$90</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Southeast Asia</td><td>$20-65</td><td>$30-95</td><td>$40-130</td><td>$60-195</td></tr>
  </table>
  <p style="font-size:.85rem;color:var(--text-light);margin-top:8px;">Fees are subject to change and vary by consulate. Express service adds $20-50. CVASC service fees ($30-60) are additional.</p>
</div></section>

<!-- Transit Visa-Free -->
<section class="section section-alt"><div class="container">
  <div class="section-header reveal">
    <h2>China Transit Visa-Free Policies</h2>
    <div class="divider"></div>
    <p>Short stays without a visa in select Chinese cities</p>
  </div>

  <p style="font-size:1.05rem;line-height:1.7;max-width:860px;margin:0 auto 32px;">China offers visa-free transit policies that allow eligible travelers from <strong>54 countries</strong> (including USA, UK, EU, Canada, Australia, Japan, South Korea, and others) to enter certain cities without a visa when transiting to a third country. This can be ideal for a quick Silk Road taster in cities like Xi'an or Beijing before continuing your journey.</p>

  <table class="visa-table">
    <tr><th>Policy</th><th>Duration</th><th>Eligible Cities/Regions</th><th>Requirements</th></tr>
    <tr>
      <td><strong>144-Hour Transit</strong></td>
      <td>Up to 6 days</td>
      <td>Beijing, Shanghai, Guangzhou, Xi'an, Chengdu, Chongqing, Hangzhou, Shenzhen, Nanjing, and more (20+ cities)</td>
      <td>Must arrive from Country A and depart to Country B (not return to A). Valid onward ticket required. Stay confined to the designated region.</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td><strong>72-Hour Transit</strong></td>
      <td>Up to 3 days</td>
      <td>Changsha, Guilin, Harbin, and select other cities</td>
      <td>Same as 144-hour policy, but limited to 72 hours and a smaller geographic area.</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td><strong>24-Hour Transit</strong></td>
      <td>Up to 1 day</td>
      <td>Most international airports in China</td>
      <td>Available to almost all nationalities. Must hold a connecting ticket to a third country departing within 24 hours.</td>
    </tr>
  </table>

  <div class="visa-note">
    <strong>&#8505;&#65039; Important:</strong> Transit visa-free is NOT available for land border crossings — it only applies at designated international airports and select cruise ports. You cannot use transit visa-free to visit Xinjiang, Tibet, Gansu, or most Silk Road destinations. For a proper Silk Road journey, a full L visa is required. Contact us if you are unsure about your eligibility.
  </div>
</div></section>

<!-- Central Asia Visa Section -->
<section class="section"><div class="container">
  <div class="section-header reveal">
    <h2>Central Asia & Neighboring Country Visas</h2>
    <div class="divider"></div>
    <p>Visa requirements for each country along the Silk Road beyond China</p>
  </div>

  <div class="visa-grid">
    
    <div class="visa-card reveal">
      <span class="visa-type evisa">E-Visa Available</span>
      <h3>&#127477;&#127487; Uzbekistan</h3>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>E-visa:</strong> Available for 90+ nationalities via official portal (e-visa.gov.uz). Processing: 3 working days, ~$20-50 depending on entries.</li>
        <li><strong>Visa-free:</strong> 30 days for 90+ countries (EU, UK, Canada, Australia, Japan, South Korea, Israel, Turkey, and more). USA citizens need an e-visa.</li>
        <li><strong>Duration:</strong> E-visa valid for 30 days, single/double/multiple entry options.</li>
        <li><strong>Registration:</strong> Hotels automatically register guests. If staying in private accommodation, register within 3 days.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>

    <div class="visa-card reveal">
      <span class="visa-type evisa">E-Visa Available</span>
      <h3>&#127472;&#127466; Kazakhstan</h3>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Visa-free:</strong> 30 days for 80+ countries including USA, UK, EU, Canada, Australia, Japan, and South Korea (since 2023).</li>
        <li><strong>E-visa:</strong> Available for nationalities requiring visas via official portal (vmp.gov.kz). Processing: 5 working days.</li>
        <li><strong>Duration:</strong> Visa-free stay up to 30 days. E-visa up to 90 days.</li>
        <li><strong>Registration:</strong> Not required for stays under 30 days under visa-free regime.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>

    <div class="visa-card reveal">
      <span class="visa-type visafree">Visa-Free (60+ countries)</span>
      <h3>&#127472;&#127474; Kyrgyzstan</h3>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Visa-free:</strong> 60 days for 60+ countries including USA, UK, EU, Canada, Australia, Japan, and South Korea.</li>
        <li><strong>E-visa:</strong> Available for countries not eligible for visa-free entry via official portal (evisa.e-gov.kg).</li>
        <li><strong>Duration:</strong> 60 days visa-free. E-visa valid for up to 90 days.</li>
        <li><strong>Registration:</strong> Required within 5 days if staying over 60 days. Hotels handle this automatically.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>

    <div class="visa-card reveal">
      <span class="visa-type evisa">E-Visa Available</span>
      <h3>&#127483;&#127479; Tajikistan</h3>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>E-visa:</strong> Available for 120+ nationalities via official portal (evisa.tj). Processing: 2-5 working days, ~$50 for GBAO permit included.</li>
        <li><strong>Visa-free:</strong> Limited to select nationalities (mostly CIS countries). Most Western travelers need an e-visa.</li>
        <li><strong>GBAO Permit:</strong> Required for Pamir Highway travel. Can be added during e-visa application ($20 extra).</li>
        <li><strong>Duration:</strong> E-visa valid for 45-60 days, single/multiple entry.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>

    <div class="visa-card reveal">
      <span class="visa-type evisa">E-Visa Available</span>
      <h3>&#127474;&#127475; Mongolia</h3>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>E-visa:</strong> Available for 100+ nationalities via official portal (evisa.mn). Processing: 3-5 working days.</li>
        <li><strong>Visa-free:</strong> 30 days for select countries (USA up to 90 days, Germany, Japan, South Korea, and others). Check eligibility.</li>
        <li><strong>Duration:</strong> E-visa valid for 30 days. Visa-free stays 30-90 days depending on nationality.</li>
        <li><strong>Registration:</strong> Required within 48 hours of arrival. Hotels and tour operators register guests.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>

    <div class="visa-card reveal">
      <span class="visa-type voa">LOI Required</span>
      <h3>&#127487;&#127474; Turkmenistan</h3>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Letter of Invitation (LOI):</strong> Required for all tourist visas. Must be obtained through a licensed tour operator before applying. We assist with LOIs through our local partners.</li>
        <li><strong>Visa on arrival:</strong> Available at Ashgabat airport with pre-approved LOI.</li>
        <li><strong>Processing:</strong> LOI takes 2-4 weeks. Embassy visa takes additional 5-10 business days.</li>
        <li><strong>Transit visa:</strong> 3-5 day transit visa available (requires valid visas for neighboring countries).</li>
      </ul>
    </div>

    <div class="visa-card reveal">
      <span class="visa-type evisa">E-Visa Available</span>
      <h3>&#127477;&#127472; Pakistan</h3>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>E-visa:</strong> Available for 190+ nationalities via official portal (visa.nadra.gov.pk). Processing: 7-10 working days.</li>
        <li><strong>Visa on arrival:</strong> Available for select nationalities (including UK, UAE, Turkey, and others) for tourism purposes.</li>
        <li><strong>Duration:</strong> Tourist visa valid for 30-90 days, single/multiple entry.</li>
        <li><strong>Karakoram Highway:</strong> For the China-Pakistan KKH route, you will need both a Chinese visa (to exit via Khunjerab Pass) and a Pakistani visa (to enter).</li>
      </ul>
    </div>

  </div>

  <div class="visa-note" style="margin-top:32px;">
    <strong>&#9888;&#65039; Important Disclaimer:</strong> Visa policies change frequently. The information above is for general guidance only and was last updated May 2026. Always verify current requirements with the relevant embassy or consulate of your destination country. Silk Road Wonders provides invitation letters and LOI assistance but is not responsible for visa application outcomes.
  </div>
</div></section>

<!-- Tibet Permit -->
<section class="section section-alt"><div class="container">
  <div class="section-header reveal">
    <h2>Tibet Travel Permit (TTP)</h2>
    <div class="divider"></div>
    <p>Special permit requirements for visiting Tibet</p>
  </div>

  <p style="font-size:1.05rem;line-height:1.7;max-width:860px;margin:0 auto 24px;">In addition to a Chinese visa, <strong>all foreign travelers must obtain a Tibet Travel Permit (TTP)</strong> to enter the Tibet Autonomous Region. This permit can only be applied for by a registered Chinese travel agency on behalf of confirmed tour clients. Individual applications are not accepted.</p>

  <div class="visa-grid" style="grid-template-columns:repeat(auto-fill,minmax(280px,1fr))">
    <div class="visa-card reveal">
      <h3>Tibet Travel Permit (TTP)</h3>
      <ul>
        <li>Required for Lhasa and all areas within the Tibet Autonomous Region</li>
        <li>Applied by us after you book a confirmed tour</li>
        <li>Processing: 8-15 business days</li>
        <li>You only need to provide: passport copy + Chinese visa copy</li>
        <li>We deliver the permit to your hotel in China before your Tibet entry</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
    <div class="visa-card reveal">
      <h3>Aliens' Travel Permit (ATP)</h3>
      <ul>
        <li>Required for areas outside Lhasa prefecture (Shigatse, Everest Base Camp, Mount Kailash, Ngari)</li>
        <li>We apply for this together with your TTP</li>
        <li>Processing: 1-3 business days (can be done locally)</li>
        <li>No additional documents needed beyond TTP requirements</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
    <div class="visa-card reveal">
      <h3>Military Permit</h3>
      <ul>
        <li>Required for sensitive border areas (Mount Kailash, Ngari, certain sections near Nepal/India border)</li>
        <li>Applied by our Lhasa office</li>
        <li>Processing: 10-15 business days</li>
        <li>We handle all military permit applications for itineraries that require them</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </div>
</div></section>

